meta {
  name: GET /v1/clients (manager cert -> 403, admin-only route)
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/clients
  body: none
  auth: none
}

assert {
  res.status: 403
  res.body.error: insufficient role
}

docs {
  Same manager identity override as manager-role-allowed.bru:

    bru run 10-auth/manager-role-forbidden.bru --env sandbox \
      --env-var baseUrl=https://test.me:8182 \
      --env-var certFile=generated/manager-client.pem \
      --env-var certKeyFile=generated/manager-client-key.pem \
      --cacert ../../work/root.pem

  GET /v1/clients requires admin -- roleSatisfies() (internal/api/auth.go)
  makes admin a strict superset of manager, never the reverse -- so a
  manager-role cert must be rejected here. This is the concrete proof
  behind the RBAC claim in README.md's route table.
}
